# stanley's bar file: ~/.config/stanley/bar, a yadm alternate per host.
#
# One widget per line, in bar order. A widget that is not listed is hidden
# and costs nothing. A blank line starts a group; groups get a wider gap, so
# gauges and bare icons do not mix.
#
#   widget[:arg]  parts...  [click: command]
#
# parts:    icon name gauge extra (none listed: every part the widget has)
# click:    each widget has its own (a popup, the volume, ...); a click:
#           command replaces it, run with BLOCK_BUTTON, BLOCK_X, BLOCK_WIDTH
# widgets:  top cpu memory disk tmp audio mic record agents messages
#           bluetooth wifi battery clock date hostname
# sections: "section left", "section center" or "section right" puts the
#           widgets after it there; before any, they are on the right. dwl
#           centres the center section and puts the left one between the
#           tags and the center. A dwl older than protocol 2 shows only the
#           right section, and draws its own clock.
# settings: set <key> <value>, for interval (ms), meter-style, meter-cells,
#           warn-at, crit-at, gap, group-gap, icon-gap
#
# Comments are whole lines only: a click command may contain '#'.
# `pkill -HUP stanley` re-reads this file.

set meter-style box

section left
hostname   name
date       extra

section center
clock      extra

section right
top        extra

cpu        icon gauge
memory     icon gauge
disk:/     icon gauge

audio      icon gauge
mic        icon name

record     icon
agents     icon
messages   icon extra
bluetooth  icon
wifi       icon
battery    icon gauge extra
